[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / [l10n](#readme) / t

###### Function: t()

## Call Signature

> **t**(`message`: `string`, ...`args`: (`string` \| `number` \| `boolean`)[]): `string`

Marks a string for localization. If a localized bundle is available for the language specified by
[env.language](#language) and the bundle has a localized value for this message, then that localized
value will be returned (with injected [args](#t) values for any templated values).

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `message` | `string` | The message to localize. Supports index templating where strings like `{0}` and `{1}` are replaced by the item at that index in the [args](#t) array. |
| ...`args` | (`string` \| `number` \| `boolean`)[] | The arguments to be used in the localized string. The index of the argument is used to match the template placeholder in the localized string. |

### Returns

`string`

localized string with injected arguments.

### Example

```ts
`l10n.t('Hello {0}!', 'World');`
```

## Call Signature

> **t**(`message`: `string`, `args`: `Record`\<`string`, `any`\>): `string`

Marks a string for localization. If a localized bundle is available for the language specified by
[env.language](#language) and the bundle has a localized value for this message, then that localized
value will be returned (with injected [args](#t-1) values for any templated values).

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `message` | `string` | The message to localize. Supports named templating where strings like `{foo}` and `{bar}` are replaced by the value in the Record for that key (foo, bar, etc). |
| `args` | `Record`\<`string`, `any`\> | The arguments to be used in the localized string. The name of the key in the record is used to match the template placeholder in the localized string. |

### Returns

`string`

localized string with injected arguments.

### Example

```ts
`l10n.t('Hello {name}', { name: 'Erich' });`
```

## Call Signature

> **t**(`options`: \{ `args?`: `Record`\<`string`, `any`\> \| (`string` \| `number` \| `boolean`)[]; `comment`: `string` \| `string`[]; `message`: `string`; \}): `string`

Marks a string for localization. If a localized bundle is available for the language specified by
[env.language](#language) and the bundle has a localized value for this message, then that localized
value will be returned (with injected args values for any templated values).

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `options` | \{ `args?`: `Record`\<`string`, `any`\> \| (`string` \| `number` \| `boolean`)[]; `comment`: `string` \| `string`[]; `message`: `string`; \} | The options to use when localizing the message. |
| `options.args?` | `Record`\<`string`, `any`\> \| (`string` \| `number` \| `boolean`)[] | The arguments to be used in the localized string. As an array, the index of the argument is used to match the template placeholder in the localized string. As a Record, the key is used to match the template placeholder in the localized string. |
| `options.comment` | `string` \| `string`[] | A comment to help translators understand the context of the message. |
| `options.message` | `string` | The message to localize. If [args](#t-2) is an array, this message supports index templating where strings like `{0}` and `{1}` are replaced by the item at that index in the [args](#t-2) array. If `args` is a `Record<string, any>`, this supports named templating where strings like `{foo}` and `{bar}` are replaced by the value in the Record for that key (foo, bar, etc). |

### Returns

`string`

localized string with injected arguments.


