[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / [workspace](#readme) / openNotebookDocument

###### Function: openNotebookDocument()

## Call Signature

> **openNotebookDocument**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`NotebookDocument`](#notebookdocument)\>

Open a notebook. Will return early if this notebook is already [loaded](#notebookdocument).
 Otherwise the notebook is loaded and the [onDidOpenNotebookDocument](#ondidopennotebookdocument)-event fires.

 Note that the lifecycle of the returned notebook is owned by the editor and not by the extension.
 That means an  [onDidCloseNotebookDocument](#ondidclosenotebookdocument)-event can occur at any time after.
 Note that opening a notebook does not show a notebook editor. This function only returns a notebook document
 which can be shown in a notebook editor but it can also be used for other things.

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The resource to open. |

### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`NotebookDocument`](#notebookdocument)\>

A promise that resolves to a [notebook](#notebookdocument).

## Call Signature

> **openNotebookDocument**(`notebookType`: `string`, `content?`: [`NotebookData`](#notebookdata)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`NotebookDocument`](#notebookdocument)\>

Open an untitled notebook. The editor will prompt the user for a file path when the document is to be saved.

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `notebookType` | `string` | The notebook type that should be used. |
| `content?` | [`NotebookData`](#notebookdata) | The initial contents of the notebook. |

### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`NotebookDocument`](#notebookdocument)\>

A promise that resolves to a [notebook](#notebookdocument).


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / [workspace](#readme) / openTextDocument

###### Function: openTextDocument()

## Call Signature

> **openTextDocument**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`TextDocument`](#textdocument)\>

Opens a document. Will return early if this document is already open. Otherwise
the document is loaded and the [didOpen](#ondidopentextdocument)-event fires.

The document is denoted by an [uri](#uri). Depending on the [scheme](#urischeme) the
following rules apply:
* `file`-scheme: Open a file on disk, will be rejected if the file does not exist or cannot be loaded.
* `untitled`-scheme: A new file that should be saved on disk, e.g. `untitled:c:\frodo\new.js`. The language
will be derived from the file name.
* For all other schemes the registered text document content [providers](#textdocumentcontentprovider) are consulted.

*Note* that the lifecycle of the returned document is owned by the editor and not by the extension. That means an
[`onDidClose`](#workspace.onDidCloseTextDocument)-event can occur at any time after opening it.

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | Identifies the resource to open. |

### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`TextDocument`](#textdocument)\>

A promise that resolves to a [document](#textdocument).

## Call Signature

> **openTextDocument**(`fileName`: `string`): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`TextDocument`](#textdocument)\>

A short-hand for `openTextDocument(Uri.file(fileName))`.

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `fileName` | `string` | A name of a file on disk. |

### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`TextDocument`](#textdocument)\>

A promise that resolves to a [document](#textdocument).

### See

openTextDocument

## Call Signature

> **openTextDocument**(`options?`: \{ `content?`: `string`; `language?`: `string`; \}): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`TextDocument`](#textdocument)\>

Opens an untitled text document. The editor will prompt the user for a file
path when the document is to be saved. The `options` parameter allows to
specify the *language* and/or the *content* of the document.

### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `options?` | \{ `content?`: `string`; `language?`: `string`; \} | Options to control how the document will be created. |
| `options.content?` | `string` | - |
| `options.language?` | `string` | - |

### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`TextDocument`](#textdocument)\>

A promise that resolves to a [document](#textdocument).


