[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / NotebookRange

### Class: NotebookRange

A notebook range represents an ordered pair of two cell indices.
It is guaranteed that start is less than or equal to end.

## Constructors

### Constructor

> **new NotebookRange**(`start`: `number`, `end`: `number`): `NotebookRange`

Create a new notebook range. If `start` is not
before or equal to `end`, the values will be swapped.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `start` | `number` | start index |
| `end` | `number` | end index. |

#### Returns

`NotebookRange`

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="end"></a> `end` | `readonly` | `number` | The exclusive end index of this range (zero-based). |
| <a id="isempty"></a> `isEmpty` | `readonly` | `boolean` | `true` if `start` and `end` are equal. |
| <a id="start"></a> `start` | `readonly` | `number` | The zero-based start index of this range. |

## Methods

### with()

> **with**(`change`: \{ `end?`: `number`; `start?`: `number`; \}): `NotebookRange`

Derive a new range for this range.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `change` | \{ `end?`: `number`; `start?`: `number`; \} | An object that describes a change to this range. |
| `change.end?` | `number` | - |
| `change.start?` | `number` | - |

#### Returns

`NotebookRange`

A range that reflects the given change. Will return `this` range if the change
is not changing anything.


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / NotebookRendererScript

