[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / FoldingRangeKind

### Enumeration: FoldingRangeKind

An enumeration of specific folding range kinds. The kind is an optional field of a [FoldingRange](#foldingrange)
and is used to distinguish specific folding ranges such as ranges originated from comments. The kind is used by commands like
`Fold all comments` or `Fold all regions`.
If the kind is not set on the range, the range originated from a syntax element other than comments, imports or region markers.

## Enumeration Members

| Enumeration Member | Value | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="comment"></a> `Comment` | `1` | Kind for folding range representing a comment. |
| <a id="imports"></a> `Imports` | `2` | Kind for folding range representing a import. |
| <a id="region"></a> `Region` | `3` | Kind for folding range representing regions originating from folding markers like `#region` and `#endregion`. |


