| <a id="beside"></a> `Beside` | `-2` | A *symbolic* editor column representing the column to the side of the active one. This value can be used when opening editors, but the *resolved* [viewColumn](#texteditorviewcolumn)-value of editors will always be `One`, `Two`, `Three`,... or `undefined` but never `Beside`. |
| <a id="eight"></a> `Eight` | `8` | The eighth editor column. |
| <a id="five"></a> `Five` | `5` | The fifth editor column. |
| <a id="four"></a> `Four` | `4` | The fourth editor column. |
| <a id="nine"></a> `Nine` | `9` | The ninth editor column. |
| <a id="one"></a> `One` | `1` | The first editor column. |
| <a id="seven"></a> `Seven` | `7` | The seventh editor column. |
| <a id="six"></a> `Six` | `6` | The sixth editor column. |
| <a id="three"></a> `Three` | `3` | The third editor column. |
| <a id="two"></a> `Two` | `2` | The second editor column. |


