[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / CustomDocumentEditEvent

### Interface: CustomDocumentEditEvent\<T\>

Event triggered by extensions to signal that an edit has occurred on an [`CustomDocument`](#CustomDocument).

## See

[CustomEditorProvider.onDidChangeCustomDocument](#customeditorproviderondidchangecustomdocument).

## Type Parameters

| Type Parameter | Default type |
| ------ | ------ |
| `T` *extends* [`CustomDocument`](#customdocument) | [`CustomDocument`](#customdocument) |

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="document"></a> `document` | `readonly` | `T` | The document that the edit is for. |
| <a id="label"></a> `label?` | `readonly` | `string` | Display name describing the edit. This will be shown to users in the UI for undo/redo operations. |

## Methods

### redo()

> **redo**(): `void` \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Redo the edit operation.

This is invoked by Theia when the user redoes this edit. To implement `redo`, your
extension should restore the document and editor to the state they were in just after this
edit was added to Theia's internal edit stack by `onDidChangeCustomDocument`.

#### Returns

`void` \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

### undo()

> **undo**(): `void` \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Undo the edit operation.

This is invoked by Theia when the user undoes this edit. To implement `undo`, your
extension should restore the document and editor to the state they were in just before this
edit was added to Theia's internal edit stack by `onDidChangeCustomDocument`.

#### Returns

`void` \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>


