[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / DiagnosticCollection

### Interface: DiagnosticCollection

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="name"></a> `name` | `readonly` | `string` | The name of this diagnostic collection, for instance `typescript`. Every diagnostic from this collection will be associated with this name. Also, the task framework uses this name when defining [problem matchers](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/tasks#_defining-a-problem-matcher). |

## Methods

### clear()

> **clear**(): `void`

Remove all diagnostics from this collection. The same
as calling `#set(undefined)`;

#### Returns

`void`

### delete()

> **delete**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): `void`

Remove all diagnostics from this collection that belong
to the provided `uri`. The same as `#set(uri, undefined)`.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | A resource identifier. |

#### Returns

`void`

### dispose()

> **dispose**(): `void`

Dispose and free associated resources. Calls
[clear](#clear).

#### Returns

`void`

### forEach()

> **forEach**(`callback`: (`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `diagnostics`: readonly [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[], `collection`: `DiagnosticCollection`) => `any`, `thisArg?`: `any`): `void`

Iterate over each entry in this collection.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `callback` | (`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `diagnostics`: readonly [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[], `collection`: `DiagnosticCollection`) => `any` | Function to execute for each entry. |
| `thisArg?` | `any` | The `this` context used when invoking the handler function. |

#### Returns

`void`

### get()

> **get**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): readonly [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[]

Get the diagnostics for a given resource. *Note* that you cannot
modify the diagnostics-array returned from this call.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | A resource identifier. |

#### Returns

readonly [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[]

An immutable array of [diagnostics](#diagnostic) or `undefined`.

### has()

> **has**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): `boolean`

Check if this collection contains diagnostics for a
given resource.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | A resource identifier. |

#### Returns

`boolean`

`true` if this collection has diagnostic for the given resource.

### set()

#### Call Signature

> **set**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `diagnostics`: [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[]): `void`

Assign diagnostics for given resource. Will replace
existing diagnostics for that resource.

##### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | A resource identifier. |
| `diagnostics` | [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[] | Array of diagnostics or `undefined` |

##### Returns

`void`

#### Call Signature

> **set**(`entries`: \[[`Uri`](#uri), [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[]\][]): `void`

Replace all entries in this collection for given uris.

Diagnostics of multiple tuples of the same uri will be merged, e.g
`[[file1, [d1]], [file1, [d2]]]` is equivalent to `[[file1, [d1, d2]]]`.
If a diagnostics item is `undefined` as in `[file1, undefined]`
all previous but not subsequent diagnostics are removed.

##### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `entries` | \[[`Uri`](#uri), [`Diagnostic`](#diagnostic)[]\][] | An array of tuples, like `[[file1, [d1, d2]], [file2, [d3, d4, d5]]]`, or `undefined`. |

##### Returns

`void`


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / Dialog

### Interface: Dialog

Common namespace for dealing with window and editor, showing messages and user input.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="ondiddispose"></a> `onDidDispose` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<`void`\> | Fired when the panel is disposed. This may be because the user closed the panel or because `.dispose()` was called on it. Trying to use the panel after it has been disposed throws an exception. |
| <a id="showoptions"></a> `showOptions?` | `readonly` | [`WebviewPanelShowOptions`](#webviewpanelshowoptions) | Settings to determine where webview panel will be reside |
| <a id="title"></a> `title` | `public` | `string` | Title of the panel shown in UI. |
| <a id="viewcolumn"></a> `viewColumn?` | `readonly` | [`ViewColumn`](#viewcolumn) | Editor position of the panel. This property is only set if the webview is in one of the editor view columns. |

## Methods

### dispose()

> **dispose**(): `void`

Dispose of the webview panel.

This closes the panel if it showing and disposes of the resources owned by the webview.
Webview panels are also disposed when the user closes the webview panel. Both cases
fire the `onDispose` event.

#### Returns

`void`

### reveal()

> **reveal**(`viewColumn?`: [`ViewColumn`](#viewcolumn), `preserveFocus?`: `boolean`): `void`

Show the webview panel in a given column.

A webview panel may only show in a single column at a time. If it is already showing, this
method moves it to a new column.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `viewColumn?` | [`ViewColumn`](#viewcolumn) | View column to show the panel in. Shows in the current `viewColumn` if undefined. |
| `preserveFocus?` | `boolean` | When `true`, the webview will not take focus. |

#### Returns

`void`


