[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / Extension

### Interface: Extension\<T\>

Represents an extension.

To get an instance of an `Extension` use [getExtension](#getextension).

## Type Parameters

| Type Parameter |
| ------ |
| `T` |

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="exports"></a> `exports` | `readonly` | `T` | The public API exported by this extension (return value of `activate`). It is an invalid action to access this field before this extension has been activated. |
| <a id="extensionkind"></a> `extensionKind` | `public` | [`ExtensionKind`](#extensionkind) | The extension kind describes if an extension runs where the UI runs or if an extension runs where the remote extension host runs. The extension kind is defined in the `package.json`-file of extensions but can also be refined via the `remote.extensionKind`-setting. When no remote extension host exists, the value is [`ExtensionKind.UI`](#extensionkindui). |
| <a id="extensionpath"></a> `extensionPath` | `readonly` | `string` | The absolute file path of the directory containing this extension. Shorthand notation for [Extension.extensionUri.fsPath](#extensionuri) (independent of the uri scheme). |
| <a id="extensionuri"></a> `extensionUri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of the directory containing the extension. |
| <a id="id"></a> `id` | `readonly` | `string` | The canonical extension identifier in the form of: `publisher.name`. |
| <a id="isactive"></a> `isActive` | `readonly` | `boolean` | `true` if the extension has been activated. |
| <a id="isfromdifferentextensionhost"></a> `isFromDifferentExtensionHost` | `readonly` | `boolean` | `true` when the extension is associated to another extension host. *Note* that an extension from another extension host cannot export API, e.g [its exports](#exports) are always `undefined`. |
| <a id="packagejson"></a> `packageJSON` | `readonly` | `any` | The parsed contents of the extension's package.json. |

## Methods

### activate()

> **activate**(): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`T`\>

Activates this extension and returns its public API.

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`T`\>

A promise that will resolve when this extension has been activated.


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / ExtensionContext

### Interface: ExtensionContext

An extension context is a collection of utilities private to an
extension.

An instance of an `ExtensionContext` is provided as the first
parameter to the `activate`-call of an extension.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="environmentvariablecollection"></a> `environmentVariableCollection` | `readonly` | [`GlobalEnvironmentVariableCollection`](#globalenvironmentvariablecollection) | Gets the extension's environment variable collection for this workspace, enabling changes to be applied to terminal environment variables. |
| <a id="extension"></a> `extension` | `readonly` | [`Extension`](#extension)\<`any`\> | The current `Extension` instance. |
| <a id="extensionmode"></a> `extensionMode` | `readonly` | [`ExtensionMode`](#extensionmode) | The mode the extension is running in. This is specific to the current extension. One extension may be in `ExtensionMode.Development` while other extensions in the host run in `ExtensionMode.Release`. |
| <a id="extensionpath"></a> `extensionPath` | `readonly` | `string` | The absolute file path of the directory containing the extension. Shorthand notation for [ExtensionContext.extensionUri.fsPath](#textdocumenturi) (independent of the uri scheme). |
| <a id="extensionuri"></a> `extensionUri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of the directory containing the extension. |
| <a id="globalstate"></a> `globalState` | `readonly` | [`Memento`](#memento) & \{ `setKeysForSync`: `void`; \} | A memento object that stores state independent of the current opened [workspace](#workspacefolders). |
| <a id="globalstoragepath"></a> ~~`globalStoragePath`~~ | `readonly` | `string` | An absolute file path in which the extension can store global state. The directory might not exist on disk and creation is up to the extension. However, the parent directory is guaranteed to be existent. Use [`globalState`](#globalstate) to store key value data. **Deprecated** Use [globalStorageUri](#globalstorageuri) instead. |
| <a id="globalstorageuri"></a> `globalStorageUri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of a directory in which the extension can store global state. The directory might not exist on disk and creation is up to the extension. However, the parent directory is guaranteed to be existent. Use [`globalState`](#globalstate) to store key value data. **See** [`workspace.fs`](#filesystem) for how to read and write files and folders from an uri. |
| <a id="languagemodelaccessinformation"></a> `languageModelAccessInformation` | `readonly` | [`LanguageModelAccessInformation`](#languagemodelaccessinformation) | An object that keeps information about how this extension can use language models. **See** [LanguageModelChat.sendRequest](#languagemodelchatsendrequest) **Stubbed** |
| <a id="logpath"></a> ~~`logPath`~~ | `readonly` | `string` | An absolute file path of a directory in which the extension can create log files. The directory might not exist on disk and creation is up to the extension. However, the parent directory is guaranteed to be existent. **Deprecated** Use [logUri](#loguri) instead. |
| <a id="loguri"></a> `logUri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of a directory in which the extension can create log files. The directory might not exist on disk and creation is up to the extension. However, the parent directory is guaranteed to be existent. **See** [`workspace.fs`](#filesystem) for how to read and write files and folders from an uri. |
| <a id="secrets"></a> `secrets` | `readonly` | [`SecretStorage`](#secretstorage) | A storage utility for secrets. Secrets are persisted across reloads and are independent of the current opened [workspace](#workspacefolders). |
| <a id="storagepath"></a> ~~`storagePath`~~ | `readonly` | `string` | An absolute file path of a workspace specific directory in which the extension can store private state. The directory might not exist on disk and creation is up to the extension. However, the parent directory is guaranteed to be existent. Use [`workspaceState`](#workspacestate) or [`globalState`](#globalstate) to store key value data. **Deprecated** Use [storageUri](#storageuri) instead. |
| <a id="storageuri"></a> `storageUri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of a workspace specific directory in which the extension can store private state. The directory might not exist and creation is up to the extension. However, the parent directory is guaranteed to be existent. The value is `undefined` when no workspace nor folder has been opened. Use [`workspaceState`](#workspacestate) or [`globalState`](#globalstate) to store key value data. **See** [`workspace.fs`](#filesystem) for how to read and write files and folders from an uri. |
| <a id="subscriptions"></a> `subscriptions` | `readonly` | \{ `dispose`: `any`; \}[] | An array to which disposables can be added. When this extension is deactivated the disposables will be disposed. *Note* that asynchronous dispose-functions aren't awaited. |
| <a id="workspacestate"></a> `workspaceState` | `readonly` | [`Memento`](#memento) | A memento object that stores state in the context of the currently opened [workspace](#workspacefolders). |

## Methods

### asAbsolutePath()

> **asAbsolutePath**(`relativePath`: `string`): `string`

Get the absolute path of a resource contained in the extension.

*Note* that an absolute uri can be constructed via [`Uri.joinPath`](#urijoinpath) and
[`extensionUri`](#extensionuri), e.g. `vscode.Uri.joinPath(context.extensionUri, relativePath);`

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `relativePath` | `string` | A relative path to a resource contained in the extension. |

#### Returns

`string`

The absolute path of the resource.


