[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / ExternalUriOpener

### Interface: ExternalUriOpener

Handles opening uris to external resources, such as http(s) links.

Extensions can implement an `ExternalUriOpener` to open `http` links to a webserver
inside of the editor instead of having the link be opened by the web browser.

Currently openers may only be registered for `http` and `https` uris.

## Methods

### canOpenExternalUri()

> **canOpenExternalUri**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `token`: [`CancellationToken`](#cancellationtoken)): [`ExternalUriOpenerPriority`](#externaluriopenerpriority) \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`ExternalUriOpenerPriority`](#externaluriopenerpriority)\>

Check if the opener can open a uri.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri being opened. This is the uri that the user clicked on. It has not yet gone through port forwarding. |
| `token` | [`CancellationToken`](#cancellationtoken) | Cancellation token indicating that the result is no longer needed. |

#### Returns

[`ExternalUriOpenerPriority`](#externaluriopenerpriority) \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`ExternalUriOpenerPriority`](#externaluriopenerpriority)\>

Priority indicating if the opener can open the external uri.

### openExternalUri()

> **openExternalUri**(`resolvedUri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `ctx`: [`OpenExternalUriContext`](#openexternaluricontext), `token`: [`CancellationToken`](#cancellationtoken)): `void` \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Open a uri.

This is invoked when:

- The user clicks a link which does not have an assigned opener. In this case, first `canOpenExternalUri`
  is called and if the user selects this opener, then `openExternalUri` is called.
- The user sets the default opener for a link in their settings and then visits a link.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `resolvedUri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri to open. This uri may have been transformed by port forwarding, so it may not match the original uri passed to `canOpenExternalUri`. Use `ctx.originalUri` to check the original uri. |
| `ctx` | [`OpenExternalUriContext`](#openexternaluricontext) | Additional information about the uri being opened. |
| `token` | [`CancellationToken`](#cancellationtoken) | Cancellation token indicating that opening has been canceled. |

#### Returns

`void` \| [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Thenable indicating that the opening has completed.


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / ExternalUriOpenerMetadata

### Interface: ExternalUriOpenerMetadata

Additional metadata about a registered `ExternalUriOpener`.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="label"></a> `label` | `readonly` | `string` | Text displayed to the user that explains what the opener does. For example, 'Open in browser preview' |
| <a id="schemes"></a> `schemes` | `readonly` | readonly `string`[] | List of uri schemes the opener is triggered for. Currently only `http` and `https` are supported. |


