[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / FileStat

### Interface: FileStat

The `FileStat`-type represents metadata about a file

## Properties

| Property | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="ctime"></a> `ctime` | `number` | The creation timestamp in milliseconds elapsed since January 1, 1970 00:00:00 UTC. |
| <a id="mtime"></a> `mtime` | `number` | The modification timestamp in milliseconds elapsed since January 1, 1970 00:00:00 UTC. *Note:* If the file changed, it is important to provide an updated `mtime` that advanced from the previous value. Otherwise there may be optimizations in place that will not show the updated file contents in an editor for example. |
| <a id="permissions"></a> `permissions?` | [`Readonly`](#filepermissionreadonly) | The permissions of the file, e.g. whether the file is readonly. *Note:* This value might be a bitmask, e.g. `FilePermission.Readonly | FilePermission.Other`. |
| <a id="size"></a> `size` | `number` | The size in bytes. *Note:* If the file changed, it is important to provide an updated `size`. Otherwise there may be optimizations in place that will not show the updated file contents in an editor for example. |
| <a id="type"></a> `type` | [`FileType`](#filetype) | The type of the file, e.g. is a regular file, a directory, or symbolic link to a file. *Note:* This value might be a bitmask, e.g. `FileType.File | FileType.SymbolicLink`. |


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / FileSystem

### Interface: FileSystem

The file system interface exposes the editor's built-in and contributed
[file system providers](#filesystemprovider). It allows extensions to work
with files from the local disk as well as files from remote places, like the
remote extension host or ftp-servers.

*Note* that an instance of this interface is available as [`workspace.fs`](#workspace.fs).

## Methods

### copy()

> **copy**(`source`: [`Uri`](#uri), `target`: [`Uri`](#uri), `options?`: \{ `overwrite?`: `boolean`; \}): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Copy files or folders.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `source` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The existing file. |
| `target` | [`Uri`](#uri) | - |
| `options?` | \{ `overwrite?`: `boolean`; \} | Defines if existing files should be overwritten. |
| `options.overwrite?` | `boolean` | - |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

### createDirectory()

> **createDirectory**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Create a new directory (Note, that new files are created via `write`-calls).

*Note* that missing directories are created automatically, e.g this call has
`mkdirp` semantics.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of the new folder. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

### delete()

> **delete**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `options?`: \{ `recursive?`: `boolean`; `useTrash?`: `boolean`; \}): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Delete a file.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The resource that is to be deleted. |
| `options?` | \{ `recursive?`: `boolean`; `useTrash?`: `boolean`; \} | Defines if trash can should be used and if deletion of folders is recursive |
| `options.recursive?` | `boolean` | - |
| `options.useTrash?` | `boolean` | - |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

### isWritableFileSystem()

> **isWritableFileSystem**(`scheme`: `string`): `boolean`

Check if a given file system supports writing files.

Keep in mind that just because a file system supports writing, that does
not mean that writes will always succeed. There may be permissions issues
or other errors that prevent writing a file.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `scheme` | `string` | The scheme of the filesystem, for example `file` or `git`. |

#### Returns

`boolean`

`true` if the file system supports writing, `false` if it does not
support writing (i.e. it is readonly), and `undefined` if the editor does not
know about the filesystem.

### readDirectory()

> **readDirectory**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<\[`string`, [`FileType`](#filetype)\][]\>

Retrieve all entries of a [directory](#filetypedirectory).

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of the folder. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<\[`string`, [`FileType`](#filetype)\][]\>

An array of name/type-tuples or a thenable that resolves to such.

### readFile()

> **readFile**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`Uint8Array`\>

Read the entire contents of a file.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of the file. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`Uint8Array`\>

An array of bytes or a thenable that resolves to such.

### rename()

> **rename**(`source`: [`Uri`](#uri), `target`: [`Uri`](#uri), `options?`: \{ `overwrite?`: `boolean`; \}): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Rename a file or folder.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `source` | [`Uri`](#uri) | - |
| `target` | [`Uri`](#uri) | - |
| `options?` | \{ `overwrite?`: `boolean`; \} | Defines if existing files should be overwritten. |
| `options.overwrite?` | `boolean` | - |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

### stat()

> **stat**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`FileStat`](#filestat)\>

Retrieve metadata about a file.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `uri` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The uri of the file to retrieve metadata about. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<[`FileStat`](#filestat)\>

The file metadata about the file.

### writeFile()

> **writeFile**(`uri`: [`Uri`](#uri), `content`: `Uint8Array`): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Write data to a file, replacing its entire contents.

#### Parameters

