[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / FileSystemProvider

### Interface: FileSystemProvider

The filesystem provider defines what the editor needs to read, write, discover,
and to manage files and folders. It allows extensions to serve files from remote places,
like ftp-servers, and to seamlessly integrate those into the editor.

* *Note 1:* The filesystem provider API works with [uris](#uri) and assumes hierarchical
paths, e.g. `foo:/my/path` is a child of `foo:/my/` and a parent of `foo:/my/path/deeper`.
* *Note 2:* There is an activation event `onFileSystem:<scheme>` that fires when a file
or folder is being accessed.
* *Note 3:* The word 'file' is often used to denote all [kinds](#filetype) of files, e.g.
folders, symbolic links, and regular files.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="ondidchangefile"></a> `onDidChangeFile` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<[`FileChangeEvent`](#filechangeevent)[]\> | An event to signal that a resource has been created, changed, or deleted. This event should fire for resources that are being [watched](#watch) by clients of this provider. *Note:* It is important that the metadata of the file that changed provides an updated `mtime` that advanced from the previous value in the [stat](#filestat) and a correct `size` value. Otherwise there may be optimizations in place that will not show the change in an editor for example. |

