| <a id="buttons"></a> `buttons` | `public` | readonly [`QuickInputButton`](#quickinputbutton)[] | Buttons for actions in the UI. | - |
| <a id="enabled"></a> `enabled` | `public` | `boolean` | If the UI should allow for user input. Defaults to true. Change this to false, e.g., while validating user input or loading data for the next step in user input. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`enabled`](#quickinputenabled) |
| <a id="ignorefocusout"></a> `ignoreFocusOut` | `public` | `boolean` | If the UI should stay open even when loosing UI focus. Defaults to false. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`ignoreFocusOut`](#quickinputignorefocusout) |
| <a id="ondidaccept"></a> `onDidAccept` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<`void`\> | An event signaling when the user indicated acceptance of the input value. | - |
| <a id="ondidchangevalue"></a> `onDidChangeValue` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<`string`\> | An event signaling when the value has changed. | - |
| <a id="ondidhide"></a> `onDidHide` | `public` | [`Event`](#event)\<`void`\> | An event signaling when this input UI is hidden. There are several reasons why this UI might have to be hidden and the extension will be notified through [QuickInput.onDidHide](#QuickInput.onDidHide). (Examples include: an explicit call to [QuickInput.hide](#QuickInput.hide), the user pressing Esc, some other input UI opening, etc.) | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`onDidHide`](#quickinputondidhide) |
| <a id="ondidtriggerbutton"></a> `onDidTriggerButton` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<[`QuickInputButton`](#quickinputbutton)\> | An event signaling when a button was triggered. | - |
| <a id="password"></a> `password` | `public` | `boolean` | If the input value should be hidden. Defaults to false. | - |
| <a id="placeholder"></a> `placeholder` | `public` | `string` | Optional placeholder in the filter text. | - |
| <a id="prompt"></a> `prompt` | `public` | `string` | An optional prompt text providing some ask or explanation to the user. | - |
| <a id="step"></a> `step` | `public` | `number` | An optional current step count. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`step`](#quickinputstep) |
| <a id="title"></a> `title` | `public` | `string` | An optional title. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`title`](#quickinputtitle) |
| <a id="totalsteps"></a> `totalSteps` | `public` | `number` | An optional total step count. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`totalSteps`](#quickinputtotalsteps) |
| <a id="validationmessage"></a> `validationMessage` | `public` | `string` \| [`InputBoxValidationMessage`](#inputboxvalidationmessage) | An optional validation message indicating a problem with the current input value. By returning a string, the InputBox will use a default [InputBoxValidationSeverity](#inputboxvalidationseverity) of Error. Returning undefined clears the validation message. | - |
| <a id="value"></a> `value` | `public` | `string` | Current input value. | - |
| <a id="valueselection"></a> `valueSelection` | `public` | readonly \[`number`, `number`\] | Selection range in the input value. Defined as tuple of two number where the first is the inclusive start index and the second the exclusive end index. When `undefined` the whole pre-filled value will be selected, when empty (start equals end) only the cursor will be set, otherwise the defined range will be selected. This property does not get updated when the user types or makes a selection, but it can be updated by the extension. | - |

## Methods

### dispose()

> **dispose**(): `void`

Dispose of this input UI and any associated resources. If it is still
visible, it is first hidden. After this call the input UI is no longer
functional and no additional methods or properties on it should be
accessed. Instead a new input UI should be created.

#### Returns

`void`

#### Inherited from

### hide()

> **hide**(): `void`

Hides this input UI. This will also fire an [QuickInput.onDidHide](#QuickInput.onDidHide)
event.

#### Returns

`void`

#### Inherited from

### show()

> **show**(): `void`

Makes the input UI visible in its current configuration. Any other input
UI will first fire an [QuickInput.onDidHide](#QuickInput.onDidHide) event.

#### Returns

`void`

