[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / NotebookCell

### Interface: NotebookCell

Represents a cell of a [notebook](#notebookdocument), either a [code](#notebookcellkindcode)-cell
or [markup](#notebookcellkindmarkup)-cell.

NotebookCell instances are immutable and are kept in sync for as long as they are part of their notebook.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="document"></a> `document` | `readonly` | [`TextDocument`](#textdocument) | The [text](#textdocument) of this cell, represented as text document. |
| <a id="executionsummary"></a> `executionSummary` | `readonly` | [`NotebookCellExecutionSummary`](#notebookcellexecutionsummary) | The most recent [execution summary](#notebookcellexecutionsummary) for this cell. |
| <a id="index"></a> `index` | `readonly` | `number` | The index of this cell in its [containing notebook](#notebookdocumentcellat). The index is updated when a cell is moved within its notebook. The index is `-1` when the cell has been removed from its notebook. |
| <a id="kind"></a> `kind` | `readonly` | [`NotebookCellKind`](#notebookcellkind) | The kind of this cell. |
| <a id="metadata"></a> `metadata` | `readonly` | \{\[`key`: `string`\]: `any`; \} | The metadata of this cell. Can be anything but must be JSON-stringifyable. |
| <a id="notebook"></a> `notebook` | `readonly` | [`NotebookDocument`](#notebookdocument) | The [notebook](#notebookdocument) that contains this cell. |
| <a id="outputs"></a> `outputs` | `readonly` | readonly [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)[] | The outputs of this cell. |


[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / NotebookCellExecution

### Interface: NotebookCellExecution

A NotebookCellExecution is how [notebook controller](#notebookcontroller) modify a notebook cell as
it is executing.

When a cell execution object is created, the cell enters the [`Pending`](#notebookcellexecutionstatepending) state.
When [`start(...)`](#start) is called on the execution task, it enters the [`Executing`](#notebookcellexecutionstateexecuting) state. When
[`end(...)`](#end) is called, it enters the [`Idle`](#notebookcellexecutionstateidle) state.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="cell"></a> `cell` | `readonly` | [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell) | The [cell](#notebookcell) for which this execution has been created. |
| <a id="executionorder"></a> `executionOrder` | `public` | `number` | Set and unset the order of this cell execution. |
| <a id="token"></a> `token` | `readonly` | [`CancellationToken`](#cancellationtoken) | A cancellation token which will be triggered when the cell execution is canceled from the UI. _Note_ that the cancellation token will not be triggered when the [controller](#notebookcontroller) that created this execution uses an [interrupt-handler](#notebookcontrollerinterrupthandler). |

## Methods

### appendOutput()

> **appendOutput**(`out`: [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)[], `cell?`: [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Append to the output of the cell that is executing or to another cell that is affected by this execution.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `out` | [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)[] | Output that is appended to the current output. |
| `cell?` | [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell) | Cell for which output is cleared. Defaults to the [cell](#cell) of this execution. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

A thenable that resolves when the operation finished.

### appendOutputItems()

> **appendOutputItems**(`items`: [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem)[], `output`: [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Append output items to existing cell output.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `items` | [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem)[] | Output items that are append to existing output. |
| `output` | [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput) | Output object that already exists. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

A thenable that resolves when the operation finished.

### clearOutput()

> **clearOutput**(`cell?`: [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Clears the output of the cell that is executing or of another cell that is affected by this execution.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `cell?` | [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell) | Cell for which output is cleared. Defaults to the [cell](#cell) of this execution. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

A thenable that resolves when the operation finished.

### end()

> **end**(`success`: `boolean`, `endTime?`: `number`): `void`

Signal that execution has ended.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `success` | `boolean` | If true, a green check is shown on the cell status bar. If false, a red X is shown. If undefined, no check or X icon is shown. |
| `endTime?` | `number` | The time that execution finished, in milliseconds in the Unix epoch. |

#### Returns

`void`

### replaceOutput()

> **replaceOutput**(`out`: [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)[], `cell?`: [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Replace the output of the cell that is executing or of another cell that is affected by this execution.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `out` | [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)[] | Output that replaces the current output. |
| `cell?` | [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell) | Cell for which output is cleared. Defaults to the [cell](#cell) of this execution. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

A thenable that resolves when the operation finished.

### replaceOutputItems()

> **replaceOutputItems**(`items`: [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem)[], `output`: [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput)): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Replace all output items of existing cell output.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `items` | [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem) \| readonly [`NotebookCellOutputItem`](#notebookcelloutputitem)[] | Output items that replace the items of existing output. |
| `output` | [`NotebookCellOutput`](#notebookcelloutput) | Output object that already exists. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

A thenable that resolves when the operation finished.

### start()

> **start**(`startTime?`: `number`): `void`

Signal that the execution has begun.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `startTime?` | `number` | The time that execution began, in milliseconds in the Unix epoch. Used to drive the clock that shows for how long a cell has been running. If not given, the clock won't be shown. |

