[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / NotebookDocument

### Interface: NotebookDocument

Represents a notebook which itself is a sequence of [code or markup cells](#notebookcell). Notebook documents are
created from [notebook data](#notebookdata).

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="cellcount"></a> `cellCount` | `readonly` | `number` | The number of cells in the notebook. |
| <a id="isclosed"></a> `isClosed` | `readonly` | `boolean` | `true` if the notebook has been closed. A closed notebook isn't synchronized anymore and won't be re-used when the same resource is opened again. |
| <a id="isdirty"></a> `isDirty` | `readonly` | `boolean` | `true` if there are unpersisted changes. |
| <a id="isuntitled"></a> `isUntitled` | `readonly` | `boolean` | Is this notebook representing an untitled file which has not been saved yet. |
| <a id="metadata"></a> `metadata` | `readonly` | \{\[`key`: `string`\]: `any`; \} | Arbitrary metadata for this notebook. Can be anything but must be JSON-stringifyable. |
| <a id="notebooktype"></a> `notebookType` | `readonly` | `string` | The type of notebook. |
| <a id="uri"></a> `uri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The associated uri for this notebook. *Note* that most notebooks use the `file`-scheme, which means they are files on disk. However, **not** all notebooks are saved on disk and therefore the `scheme` must be checked before trying to access the underlying file or siblings on disk. **See** [FileSystemProvider](#filesystemprovider) |
| <a id="version"></a> `version` | `readonly` | `number` | The version number of this notebook (it will strictly increase after each change, including undo/redo). |

## Methods

### cellAt()

> **cellAt**(`index`: `number`): [`NotebookCell`](#notebookcell)

Return the cell at the specified index. The index will be adjusted to the notebook.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `index` | `number` | The index of the cell to retrieve. |

#### Returns

A [cell](#notebookcell).

### getCells()

