[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / QuickPick

### Interface: QuickPick\<T\>

A concrete [QuickInput](#quickinput) to let the user pick an item from a
list of items of type T. The items can be filtered through a filter text field and
there is an option [canSelectMany](#canselectmany) to allow for
selecting multiple items.

Note that in many cases the more convenient [window.showQuickPick](#window.showQuickPick)
is easier to use. [window.createQuickPick](#window.createQuickPick) should be used
when [window.showQuickPick](#window.showQuickPick) does not offer the required flexibility.

## Extends

- [`QuickInput`](#quickinput)

## Type Parameters

| Type Parameter |
| ------ |
| `T` *extends* [`QuickPickItem`](#quickpickitem) |

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description | Inherited from |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="activeitems"></a> `activeItems` | `public` | readonly `T`[] | Active items. This can be read and updated by the extension. | - |
| <a id="busy"></a> `busy` | `public` | `boolean` | If the UI should show a progress indicator. Defaults to false. Change this to true, e.g., while loading more data or validating user input. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`busy`](#quickinputbusy) |
| <a id="buttons"></a> `buttons` | `public` | readonly [`QuickInputButton`](#quickinputbutton)[] | Buttons for actions in the UI. | - |
| <a id="canselectmany"></a> `canSelectMany` | `public` | `boolean` | If multiple items can be selected at the same time. Defaults to false. | - |
| <a id="enabled"></a> `enabled` | `public` | `boolean` | If the UI should allow for user input. Defaults to true. Change this to false, e.g., while validating user input or loading data for the next step in user input. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`enabled`](#quickinputenabled) |
| <a id="ignorefocusout"></a> `ignoreFocusOut` | `public` | `boolean` | If the UI should stay open even when loosing UI focus. Defaults to false. | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`ignoreFocusOut`](#quickinputignorefocusout) |
| <a id="items"></a> `items` | `public` | readonly `T`[] | Items to pick from. | - |
| <a id="keepscrollposition"></a> `keepScrollPosition?` | `public` | `boolean` | - | - |
| <a id="matchondescription"></a> `matchOnDescription` | `public` | `boolean` | If the filter text should also be matched against the description of the items. Defaults to false. | - |
| <a id="matchondetail"></a> `matchOnDetail` | `public` | `boolean` | If the filter text should also be matched against the detail of the items. Defaults to false. | - |
| <a id="ondidaccept"></a> `onDidAccept` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<`void`\> | An event signaling when the user indicated acceptance of the selected item(s). | - |
| <a id="ondidchangeactive"></a> `onDidChangeActive` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<readonly `T`[]\> | An event signaling when the active items have changed. | - |
| <a id="ondidchangeselection"></a> `onDidChangeSelection` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<readonly `T`[]\> | An event signaling when the selected items have changed. | - |
| <a id="ondidchangevalue"></a> `onDidChangeValue` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<`string`\> | An event signaling when the value of the filter text has changed. | - |
| <a id="ondidhide"></a> `onDidHide` | `public` | [`Event`](#event)\<`void`\> | An event signaling when this input UI is hidden. There are several reasons why this UI might have to be hidden and the extension will be notified through [QuickInput.onDidHide](#QuickInput.onDidHide). (Examples include: an explicit call to [QuickInput.hide](#QuickInput.hide), the user pressing Esc, some other input UI opening, etc.) | [`QuickInput`](#quickinput).[`onDidHide`](#quickinputondidhide) |
| <a id="ondidtriggerbutton"></a> `onDidTriggerButton` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<[`QuickInputButton`](#quickinputbutton)\> | An event signaling when a button was triggered. | - |
| <a id="ondidtriggeritembutton"></a> `onDidTriggerItemButton` | `readonly` | [`Event`](#event)\<[`QuickPickItemButtonEvent`](#quickpickitembuttonevent)\<`T`\>\> | An event signaling when a button in a particular [QuickPickItem](#quickpickitem) was triggered. This event does not fire for buttons in the title bar. | - |
| <a id="placeholder"></a> `placeholder` | `public` | `string` | Optional placeholder in the filter text. | - |
| <a id="selecteditems"></a> `selectedItems` | `public` | readonly `T`[] | Selected items. This can be read and updated by the extension. | - |
