| <a id="backgroundcolor"></a> `backgroundColor` | `public` | [`ThemeColor`](#themecolor) | The background color for this entry. *Note*: only the following colors are supported: * `new ThemeColor('statusBarItem.errorBackground')` * `new ThemeColor('statusBarItem.warningBackground')` More background colors may be supported in the future. *Note*: when a background color is set, the statusbar may override the `color` choice to ensure the entry is readable in all themes. |
| <a id="color"></a> `color` | `public` | `string` \| [`ThemeColor`](#themecolor) | The foreground color for this entry. |
| <a id="command"></a> `command` | `public` | `string` \| [`Command`](#command) | The identifier of a command to run on click. |
| <a id="id"></a> `id` | `readonly` | `string` | The identifier of this item. *Note*: if no identifier was provided by the [`window.createStatusBarItem`](#createstatusbaritem) method, the identifier will match the [extension identifier](#extensionid). |
| <a id="name"></a> `name` | `public` | `string` | The name of the entry, like 'Python Language Indicator', 'Git Status' etc. Try to keep the length of the name short, yet descriptive enough that users can understand what the status bar item is about. |
| <a id="priority"></a> `priority` | `readonly` | `number` | The priority of this item. Higher value means the item should be shown more to the left. |
| <a id="text"></a> `text` | `public` | `string` | The text to show for the entry. To set a text with icon use the following pattern in text string: $(fontawesomeClassName) |
| <a id="tooltip"></a> `tooltip` | `public` | `string` \| [`MarkdownString`](#markdownstring) | The tooltip text when you hover over this entry. |

