## Methods

### dispose()

> **dispose**(): `void`

Dispose this object.

#### Returns

`void`

#### Inherited from

### reveal()

> **reveal**(`element`: `T`, `options?`: \{ `expand?`: `number` \| `boolean`; `focus?`: `boolean`; `select?`: `boolean`; \}): [`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>

Reveals the given element in the tree view.
If the tree view is not visible then the tree view is shown and element is revealed.

By default revealed element is selected.
In order to not to select, set the option `select` to `false`.
In order to focus, set the option `focus` to `true`.
In order to expand the revealed element, set the option `expand` to `true`. To expand recursively set `expand` to the number of levels to expand.

* *NOTE:* In VS Code, you can expand only to 3 levels maximum. This is not the case in Theia, there are no limits to expansion level.
* *NOTE:* The [TreeDataProvider](#treedataprovider) that the `TreeView` [is registered with](#createtreeview) with must implement [getParent](#treedataprovidergetparent) method to access this API.

#### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| `element` | `T` | - |
| `options?` | \{ `expand?`: `number` \| `boolean`; `focus?`: `boolean`; `select?`: `boolean`; \} | - |
| `options.expand?` | `number` \| `boolean` | If true, then the element will be expanded. If a number is passed, then up to that number of levels of children will be expanded |
| `options.focus?` | `boolean` | If true, then the element will be focused. |
| `options.select?` | `boolean` | If true, then the element will be selected. |

#### Returns

[`Thenable`](#thenable)\<`void`\>


