[@baosky/plugin](#readme) / WorkspaceFolder

### Interface: WorkspaceFolder

A workspace folder is one of potentially many roots opened by the editor. All workspace folders
are equal which means there is no notion of an active or master workspace folder.

## Properties

| Property | Modifier | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| <a id="index"></a> `index` | `readonly` | `number` | The ordinal number of this workspace folder. |
| <a id="name"></a> `name` | `readonly` | `string` | The name of this workspace folder. Defaults to the basename of its [uri-path](#Uri.path) |
| <a id="uri"></a> `uri` | `readonly` | [`Uri`](#uri) | The associated uri for this workspace folder. *Note:* The [Uri](#uri)-type was intentionally chosen such that future releases of the editor can support workspace folders that are not stored on the local disk, e.g. `ftp://server/workspaces/foo`. |


